rect:\n\nActually, the general equation of a circle through A(0,0) and B(1,0) is x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 + l x + m y + n = 0. Since it passes through (0,0), n = 0. Passing through (1,0): 1 + 0 + l(1) + 0 + 0 = 0 \u21d2 1 + l = 0 \u21d2 l = -1. So the equation is x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 - x + m y = 0. So both \u0393\u2081 and \u0393\u2082 have equations of this form, with different m. Let\u2019s say \u0393\u2081 has m = m\u2081 and \u0393\u2082 has m = m\u2082. Therefore:\n\n\u0393\u2081: x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 - x + m\u2081 y = 0\n\n\u0393\u2082: x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 - x + m\u2082 y = 0\n\nNow, line d is parametrized as (t cos\u03b8, t sin\u03b8). Let's find point P on \u0393\u2081. Substitute x = t cos\u03b8, y = t sin\u03b8 into \u0393\u2081's equation:\n\n(t cos\u03b8)\u00b2 + (t sin\u03b8)\u00b2 - t cos\u03b8 + m\u2081 (t sin\u03b8) = 0\n\nSimplify:\n\nt\u00b2 (cos\u00b2\u03b8 + sin\u00b2\u03b8) - t cos\u03b8 + m\u2081 t sin\u03b8 = 0\n\nSince cos\u00b2\u03b8 + sin\u00b2\u03b8 = 1:\n\nt\u00b2 - t cos\u03b8 + m\u2081 t sin\u03b8 = 0\n\nFactor t:\n\nt (t - cos\u03b8 + m\u2081 sin\u03b8) = 0\n\nSolutions at t = 0 (point A) and t = cos\u03b8 - m\u2081 sin\u03b8. So point P is at t = cos\u03b8 - m\u2081 sin\u03b8:\n\nP = ( (cos\u03b8 - m\u2081 sin\u03b8) cos\u03b8, (cos\u03b8 - m\u2081 sin\u03b8) sin\u03b8 )\n\nSimilarly, point Q is on \u0393\u2082. Substitute into \u0393\u2082's equation:\n\n(t cos\u03b8)^2 + (t sin\u03b8)^2 - t cos\u03b8 + m\u2082 (t sin\u03b8) = 0\n\nSimilarly:\n\nt\u00b2 - t cos\u03b8 + m\u2082 t sin\u03b8 = 0\n\nSolutions t = 0 and t = cos\u03b8 - m\u2082 sin\u03b8. So Q is at:\n\nQ = ( (cos\u03b8 - m\u2082 sin\u03b8) cos\u03b8, (cos\u03b8 - m\u2082 sin\u03b8) sin\u03b8 )\n\nSimilarly, for line d' passing through B(1,0) with direction (cos\u03c6, sin\u03c6), parametrized as (1 + s cos\u03c6, 0 + s sin\u03c6). Let's find P' on \u0393\u2081:\n\nSubstitute x = 1 + s cos\u03c6, y = s sin\u03c6 into \u0393\u2081's equation:\n\n(1 + s cos\u03c6)^2 + (s sin\u03c6)^2 - (1 