ope QQ' = [ C + m\u2082 D ] / [ E + m\u2082 F ]\n\nWhere:\n\nC = - sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 - sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8\n\nD = sin\u00b2\u03b8 - sin\u00b2\u03c6\n\nE = 1 - cos\u00b2\u03c6 - cos\u00b2\u03b8\n\nF = sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8 - sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6\n\nSo, unless (C + m\u2081 D)/(E + m\u2081 F) = (C + m\u2082 D)/(E + m\u2082 F) for all m\u2081, m\u2082, which would require that the function f(m) = (C + m D)/(E + m F) is constant for all m, which would require D/E = C/F and D/F = C/E, which seems unlikely unless C, D, E, F have specific relations.\n\nAlternatively, if the function f(m) is the same for any m, then:\n\n(C + m D)(E + m' F) = (C + m' D)(E + m F)\n\nExpanding both sides:\n\nC E + C m' F + m D E + m m' D F = C E + C m F + m' D E + m m' D F\n\nSubtract common terms:\n\nC m' F + m D E = C m F + m' D E\n\nRearranged:\n\nC m' F - C m F = m' D E - m D E\n\nFactor:\n\nC F (m' - m) = D E (m' - m)\n\nThus, for m \u2260 m', we have C F = D E\n\nSo unless C F = D E, the equality would not hold for arbitrary m\u2081 and m\u2082.\n\nTherefore, if C F = D E, then regardless of m, the slope would be the same.\n\nSo let's check if C F = D E.\n\nCompute C F:\n\nC = - sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 - sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8\n\nF = sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8 - sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6\n\nThus, C F = (- sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 - sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8)(sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8 - sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 )\n\n= (- sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6)(sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8) + (- sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6)(- sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6) + (- sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8)(sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8) + (- sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8)(- sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 )\n\n= - sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8 + sin\u00b2\u03c6 cos\u00b2\u03c6 - sin\u00b2\u03b8 cos\u00b2\u03b8 + sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8 sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6\n\nSimplify:\n\nThe first and last terms cancel: - sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8 + sin\u03b8 cos\u03b8 sin\u03c6 cos\u03c6 = 0\n\nMiddle terms: sin\u00b2\u03c6 cos\u00b2\u03c6 - sin\u00b2\u03b8 cos\u00b2\u03b8\n\nSo C F = sin\u00b2\u03c6 cos\u00b2\u03c6 - sin\u00b2\u