 \\boxed{\\dfrac{1}{4}}.", "deepseek_solution": "Given the quadratic function \\( f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \\) with the conditions \\( f(-1) = 0 \\) and \\( x \\leq f(x) \\leq \\frac{1}{2}(x^2 + 1) \\) for all \\( x \\in \\mathbb{R} \\), we need to find the value of \\( a \\).\n\n1. From \\( f(-1) = 0 \\):\n   \\[\n   a(-1)^2 + b(-1) + c = 0 \\implies a - b + c = 0 \\implies c = b - a.\n   \\]\n\n2. For the inequality \\( x \\leq f(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   ax^2 + bx + c \\geq x \\implies ax^2 + (b - 1)x + c \\geq 0.\n   \\]\n   This quadratic must be non-negative for all \\( x \\), leading to:\n   - Leading coefficient \\( a > 0 \\)\n   - Discriminant \\( (b - 1)^2 - 4ac \\leq 0 \\).\n\n3. For the inequality \\( f(x) \\leq \\frac{1}{2}(x^2 + 1) \\):\n   \\[\n   ax^2 + bx + c \\leq \\frac{1}{2}(x^2 + 1) \\implies (a - \\frac{1}{2})x^2 + bx + (c - \\frac{1}{2}) \\leq 0.\n   \\]\n   This quadratic must be non-positive for all \\( x \\), leading to:\n   - Leading coefficient \\( a < \\frac{1}{2} \\)\n   - Discriminant \\( b^2 - 4(a - \\frac{1}{2})(c - \\frac{1}{2}) \\leq 0 \\).\n\nSubstituting \\( c = b - a \\) into the discriminant conditions and simplifying, we introduce \\( t = 2a - b \\). This leads to:\n- For the first discriminant: \\( t^2 - 4a + 2t + 1 \\leq 0 \\)\n- For the second discriminant: \\( t^2 + 4a - 2t - 1 \\leq 0 \\)\n\nAdding these inequalities:\n\\[\n2t^2 \\leq 0 \\implies t = 0 \\implies b = 2a.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( b = 2a \\) and \\( c = a \\) into the inequalities:\n- From \\( a > 0 \\) and \\( a < \\frac{1}{2} \\), we get \\( 0 < a < \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n- The discriminants simplify to \\( a \\geq \\frac{1}{4} \\) and \\( a \\leq \\frac{1}{4} \\), leading to \\( a = \\frac{1}{4} \\).\n\nVerification shows that \\( a = \\frac{1}{4} \\) satisfies all conditions, making the quadratic function \\( f(x) = \\frac{1}{4}x^2 + \\frac{1}{2}x + \\frac{1}{4} \\) meet the given inequalities.\n\nThe value of \\( a \\) is \\boxed{\\dfrac{1}{4}}.", "ground_truth_solut