*205 yuan**.", "ground_truth_solution": "1. First, let\u2019s define the piecewise function \\( f(x) \\) that represents the tax calculation based on the given tax rates for different income brackets.\n\n$$ f(x) = \\begin{cases} \n5\\% \\cdot x & \\text{if } 0 < x \\leq 500 \\\\\n10\\% \\cdot (x - 500) + 500 \\cdot 5\\% & \\text{if } 500 < x \\leq 2000 \\\\\n15\\% \\cdot (x - 2000) + 1500 \\cdot 10\\% + 500 \\cdot 5\\% & \\text{if } 2000 < x \\leq 5000\n\\end{cases} $$\n\nThis function breaks down as follows:\n- For \\( 0 < x \\leq 500 \\), the tax rate is 5%.\n- For \\( 500 < x \\leq 2000 \\), the tax rate for the amount above 500 is 10%, and the tax for the first 500 is already calculated.\n- For \\( 2000 < x \\leq 5000 \\), the tax rate for the amount above 2000 is 15%, plus the calculated tax for the first 2000.\n\n2. Given that an individual\u2019s total monthly income in March 2000 is 3000 yuan, the taxable income (after subtracting the 800 yuan deductible) is:\n\n$$ x = 3000 - 800 = 2200 $$\n\n3. We need to determine which tax bracket this income falls under. Since \\( 2000 < 2200 \\leq 5000 \\), the third case of the piecewise function applies. \n\n4. Applying the third case of the function \\( f(x) \\):\n\n\\[\nf(2200) = 15\\% \\cdot (2200 - 2000) + 1500 \\cdot 10\\% + 500 \\cdot 5\\%\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term individually:\n\n\\[\n15\\% \\cdot (2200 - 2000) = 0.15 \\cdot 200 = 30\n\\]\n\n\\[\n1500 \\cdot 10\\% = 0.10 \\cdot 1500 = 150\n\\]\n\n\\[\n500 \\cdot 5\\% = 0.05 \\cdot 500 = 25\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\n\\[\nf(2200) =  30 + 150 + 25 = 205\n\\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nTherefore, the amount of individual income tax to be paid for March 2000 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{205 \\text{ yuan}}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}]